course: dictionary
lesson: 13495
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Illumination is one of them. «The room needs better illumination» is about light, but «Her talk gave us some illumination» is about understanding.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. If the sentence is about lamps, bulbs or dark rooms, illumination means light. If it is about an idea becoming clear, it means understanding. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Illumination can also mean coloured lights put up to decorate a town, as in «We walked along the front to see the Blackpool Illuminations.» The clue is the plural, illuminations, and the lights for a festival at a seaside town.
fact: Illumination means light, or lighting up a place.
fact: In Britain, the illuminations are coloured lights used to decorate a town or seaside, often for a festival.
fact: Illumination can also mean understanding or explaining something, as in «Her talk gave us some illumination».
fact: An illumination can be a painted, coloured picture or letter in an old handwritten book, like the ones monks made.
fact: Illumination is usually uncountable, so you say «some illumination», but one painted picture in an old book is «an illumination».
exercise: «The room needs better illumination.» What does illumination mean here? | *Light, or lighting up a place | A painted picture in an old book | A loud noise | Understanding something new
exercise: «We walked along the front to see the Blackpool Illuminations.» What are the illuminations? | Painted letters in an old book | Clever explanations | Dark, quiet streets | *Coloured lights that decorate a town
exercise: «Her talk gave us some illumination about how the brain works.» What does illumination mean here? | Light from a lamp | A coloured picture | *Understanding or explaining something | A loud shout
test: The monk spent months painting an illumination in the old book. What is an illumination here? | *A painted, coloured picture in a handwritten book | A town lit up at night | Understanding of a story | Light from a torch
test: «Street illumination kept the park safe after dark.» What does illumination mean? | A big, loud crowd | *Light that lets you see | A painted letter | Understanding why something happened
exam: Which meaning of illumination fits «The scientist measured the illumination on the desk with a light meter»? | A painted letter in an old book | Coloured lights for a festival | *Amount of light falling on something | Understanding something new
